#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176047 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175693 :question/id #uuid "70569afd-42c4-5e5f-8397-4fbd873eb8e4" :question/math-academy-id "e-11002" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\cos x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The range of the function is $[-1,1].$\n\n- The function has minimum values at $x =n\\pi.$\n\n- The function intersects the $x$-axis at $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2} +\\pi n.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's plot the graph of $y=\\cos{x}.$\n\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The minimum value is $-1,$ and the maximum value is $1.$ Therefore, the range is $[-1,1].$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function has a minimum at $x=\\pi$ and the period is $2\\pi.$ Therefore, the minimum values occur at $\\pi+2n\\pi.$\n\n- Statement III is true. These are the zeros of the cosine curve. The cosine curve has zeros at $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2} + n\\pi.$\n\nIn conclusion, only statements I and III are true."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "542df339-5020-5680-a39c-a1ae161083e7" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050033 :topic/id #uuid "27991def-afa0-5245-84f6-cb161dd1a2bc" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152178} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152216} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152217} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152218}] :topic/math-academy-id 2707 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049075} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049091} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050172} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050713}] :topic/title "Local Extrema of Functions"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050718 :topic/id #uuid "61092d2e-5ae6-5f60-8a88-2299822508ec" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110576} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110577} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110578} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110579}] :topic/math-academy-id 1491 :topic/next [{:db