      \n                                        \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n{{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$).$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \nThe range of the function is $[$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n{{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n{{field-4}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$].$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The period of the function is\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n{{field-5}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=sin⁡x.$\n\n![](images/96/96bd60d23237f836b77a26c5c0461a5c2a474554f0a14266b53fc5e7d999f1b7.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n* The domain of the function is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n* The minimum value is $-1,$ and the maximum value is $1.$ Therefore, the range is $[-1,1].$\n\n* The period of $sin⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237982 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bdd8d5ad-073e-55ee-92c1-3d941cfbf8cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437300} {:answer/id #uuid "62442bed-3629-535b-844a-f1ed8cc3a547" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437301}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62442bed-3629-535b-844a-f1ed8cc3a547" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437301} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b115472-4d06-5a5e-9cd3-15210c6010e5" :answer-field/key "The function is zero at $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438679} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7edfcf80-e21f-5e22-8902-7e7b1332485b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437302} {:answer/id #uuid "9c74c49e-6c9c-5bab-9fb2-8efb50f61131" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437303}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7edfcf80-e21f-5e22-8902-7e7b1332485b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437302} :answer-field/id #uuid "9da1c4d9-8e1c-5e3d-8925-a2ad4ef01523" :answer-field/key "Its range is $y\\in [-2,2]$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438680} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57a3617f-5ddc-5f1e-9587-578cb2e5daae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437304} {:answer/id #uuid "8c3927d0-6855-5216-a9b2-c6bb7f951391" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57a3617f-5ddc-5f1e-9587-578cb2e5daae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437304} :answer-field/id #uuid "e42ef86b-359c-5579-8280-6358310897d5" :answer-field/key "$y=-\\frac{3}{2}$ is an output of the function" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438681}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4817b633-1cdd-52d9-b9a7-098236a7867f" :question/math-academy-id "q-103230" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=cos⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=cos⁡x.$\n\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement “The function is zero at $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$” is true. At $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$, the function $y=cos⁡x$ takes the value zero.\n\n- Statements “Its range is $y\\in [-2,2]$” and “$y=-\\frac{3}{2}$ is 