roblem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\cos x$? Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\cos x$.\n\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement “The complete set of inputs at which the function has zeros is $x=n\\pi.$” is false. The zeros occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi$. Every zero must be included.\n\n- Statement “The complete set of inputs at which the function has maximum values is $x=n\\pi.$” is false. The maximum value is $1$, attained at $x=2n\\pi$. Every maximum input must be included.\n\n- Statement “The complete set of inputs at which the function has minimum values is $x=\\pi+2n\\pi.$” is true. The minimum value is $-1$, attained at $x=\\pi+2n\\pi$. Every minimum input must be included."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186580892 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66ee4154-2c82-5f7c-a453-639a3c26e78e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580557} {:answer/id #uuid "a4446db1-6811-56cb-83ad-f4290b765162" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580661} {:answer/id #uuid "dc264dd9-aead-5752-b49e-de8c3a93172a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580731} {:answer/id #uuid "e0766b7f-1b11-54db-a463-de8434f00db9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580738} {:answer/id #uuid "ee1767e8-6b16-5f29-a9f2-9d13c262d7a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc264dd9-aead-5752-b49e-de8c3a93172a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580731} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfdb6ef3-805b-5c90-be75-327e320d6c71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580858}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "24945ccb-291e-5b02-a82c-6983ca8e2098" :question/math-academy-id "q-27019" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=0$ for $$\n\\displaystyle x=\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pm \\frac{3\\pi }{2},....\n$$\n\nII. $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ has a minimum value at $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{2}$, which is equal to $-1.$\n\nIII. The range of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is $[-1,1].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The zeros of the function $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ occur at $\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi$ for any integer $n.$\n\n- Statement II is false. $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{2}$ is a zero of the function.\n\n- Statement III is true. The minimum value is $-1$, the maximum value is $1$, and so the range is $[-1,1].$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186580899 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dd1d219-b857-5b5f-a779-302045da7712" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580408} {:answer/id #uuid "3ffe0c79-47de-5b14-88c0-6da61308e7b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580494} {:answer/id #uuid "a2a27c37-36e7-5f80-87f2-d34f3be666ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580660} {:answer/id #uuid "b8c7ebfd-c5dc-51d3-95b8-c30068e3aa83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580684} {:answer/id #uuid "c39b7953-b317-5f0e-8c8a-8e4d700894fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2a27c37-36e7-5f80-87f2-d34f3be666ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580660} :answer-field/id #uuid "f73fd2d0-ce67-564f-8d0c-066bb7ff774e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580877}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3cfbb3ff-1787-5500-ba6b-0a0c378c7517" :question/math-academy-id "q-103227" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x?$ \n\nI. The function intersects the $x$-axis at $x=2\\pi$\n\nII. Its minimum value is $-1$\n\nIII. The function intersects the $y$-axis at $y=1$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\pi =1\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the minimum value of the function is $-1.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function intersects the $y$-axis at $y=1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186580956 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2153b638-5a48-5879-a797-f45755fef1c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580438} {:answer/id #uuid "415f1c04-3325-5c6c-9e37-199d76af8270" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580496} {:answer/id #uuid "9d4862ee-2fd3-59d7-a815-add17575e836" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580652} {:answer/id #uuid "c795e8ee-d9cc-5b4e-9318-6c3d73a0a57c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580698} {:answer/id #uuid "ccbf85bc-ebfa-5124-998d-be2debcef7d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580708}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2153b638-5a48-5879-a797-f45755fef1c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580438} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1ed5084-2ed3-5f3c-8c8a-972f5c48d95c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186580859}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e9a2e847-6e9d-5334-8d47-3c2e8d9dab70" :question/math-academy-id "q-103219" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nI. The function reaches its minimum value at $x=2n\\pi$\n\nII. The zeros of the function are $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\nIII. The range of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is $[-1,0].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/04/04f13f2dec860874174f51990f4260615e7be893a6be5f86b3b13857c4e8953f.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function reaches its minimum value at $x=\\pi \\pm 2\\pi ,\\pi \\pm 4\\pi ,…,$ which can be written as $x=\\pi +2n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is true. The zeros occur at $$\n\\displaystyle x=\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pm \\frac{3\\pi }{2},…,\n$$ which can be written as $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement III is false. The minimum value is $-1$, the maximum value is $1$, and so the range is $[-1,1].$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186581724 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "234fbd64-3e71-5154-ba26-c33ca9ec6950" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581076}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "234fbd64-3e71-5154-ba26-c33ca9ec6950" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581076} :answer-field/id #uuid "32061a8c-5090-50ce-ba79-da5f40f5cbb1" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581529} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3aeab3b-a5ca-5a04-bcdb-bed224c74207" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581481}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3aeab3b-a5ca-5a04-bcdb-bed224c74207" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581481} :answer-field/id #uuid "727182ea-b0dc-5650-931f-1144963d2573" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581561} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb6337cc-bf42-5a29-9bf5-2dc359f58d8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb6337cc-bf42-5a29-9bf5-2dc359f58d8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581467} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a9965c6-ca41-50a9-81f8-b456e5eca1c7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581581} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9315993c-5171-5b3f-94b3-42d7c3c23737" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581287}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9315993c-5171-5b3f-94b3-42d7c3c23737" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581287} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2515abb-3b8d-5ba1-84a6-8154a443be88" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581585} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4afb0a0e-82c0-5586-856c-f6410ae81b8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4afb0a0e-82c0-5586-856c-f6410ae81b8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581156} :answer-field/id #uuid "d76c56e7-b4cc-5cbe-a907-4b7404595cc6" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186581611}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bac76f4a-4116-5fca-a94a-36ce5cbe8b54" :question/math-academy-id "q-167583" :question/problem "Complete the following facts about the function $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\nThe domain of the function is $x\\in ($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$\n\nThe range of the function is $[$\n{{field-3}}\n$,$\n{{field-4}}\n$].$\n\nThe period of the function is\n{{field-5}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/96/96bd60d23237f836b77a26c5c0461a5c2a474554f0a14266b53fc5e7d999f1b7.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n* The domain of the function is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n* The minimum value is $-1,$ and the maximum value is $1.$ Therefore, the range is $[-1,1].$\n\n* The period of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186585738 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ab5cdca-189e-52b2-be54-a0503ca79375" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186585397}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ab5cdca-189e-52b2-be54-a0503ca79375" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186585397} :answer-field/id #uuid "26ba861f-b15d-52e9-8a84-3a7d609f4655" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186585609} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "417289e7-c73a-5143-86c0-e7e05ba57000" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186585299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "417289e7-c73a-5143-86c0-e7e05ba57000" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186585299} :answer-field/id #uuid "35efb24a-9e94-5377-b7da-2b0ab09e50f5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186585616} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a7dc364-5a72-58cf-815e-4e86750bd04e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186585260}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a7dc364-5a72-58cf-815e-4e86750bd04e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186585260} :answer-field/id #uuid "55aa2ba0-d01d-5f53-89a6-8e83b2a3c1c6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186585632} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af9c512a-03d5-54ac-b2a9-8c61ffa45614" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186585482}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af9c512a-03d5-54ac-b2a9-8c61ffa45614" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186585482} :answer-field/id #uuid "6407632e-5356-5c51-949f-e505f5602aa1" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186585638} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a5cb174-5766-5bd4-93bd-41748015067f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186585259}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a5cb174-5766-5bd4-93bd-41748015067f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186585259} :answer-field/id #uuid "80bbfc2a-a5e7-5f5d-a854-bfe10f2ea1cd" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186585644}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2b74a3d3-c29e-513b-a913-e51860e5cc88" :question/math-academy-id "q-167613" :question/problem "Complete the following facts about the function $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\nThe domain of the function is $x\\in ($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$\n\nThe range of the function is $[$\n{{field-3}}\n$,$\n{{field-4}}\n$].$\n\nThe period of the function is\n{{field-5}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ \n\n![](images/ce/cebd0527c2b8b3bcdf2948da0771103f17412ff058d74b96db1287a7046ba3bc.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n* The domain of the function is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n* The minimum value is $-1,$ and the maximum value is $1.$ Therefore, the range is $[-1,1].$\n\n* The period of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186619728 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "213a4c1d-b52e-5221-8ad6-bafab66ca787" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619213} {:answer/id #uuid "34f2c4fa-9589-5f3b-a92d-7ab1dfecb4ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619254} {:answer/id #uuid "5e47ffcf-8937-546e-86c3-086790f1ca96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619313} {:answer/id #uuid "6ef1a6af-af24-5d21-9979-34303223d001" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619343} {:answer/id #uuid "b02b9187-1038-564f-a7c8-07dfab96ffd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619453}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e47ffcf-8937-546e-86c3-086790f1ca96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619313} :answer-field/id #uuid "48d39eb1-5500-5131-a5b1-8eba2c1dc701" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619626}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "28614a2a-126b-5809-92bc-8cfc91edc708" :question/math-academy-id "q-27012" :question/problem "Which of the following statements regarding the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ are true?\n\nI. The graph intersects the $x$-axis at $x=\\pi .$\n\nII. $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ has a minimum value at $x=\\pi$, which is equal to $-1.$\n\nIII. The range of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is $[-1,1].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. As $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )=-1$, $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ does not intersect the $x$-axis at $x=\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function has a minimum at $x=\\pi$ and the value of the minimum is $-1.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The minimum value is $-1$, the maximum value is $1$, and so the range is $[-1,1]$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Cosine Function"}]}
